# Push changes to GitHub

When you finish a task that edits project files (not only answering questions), **commit** those changes with a clear message and **`git push`** to `origin` on the current branch (usually `main`), unless the user explicitly asked not to push or there is no remote.

If `git push` fails (auth, conflicts), report the error and what is needed to fix it; do not claim the push succeeded.
